{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## AWAITING USER DECISION — pydantic-ai v2 OpenAI API semantics\n\nEvidence: current tests exercise custom OpenAI-compatible endpoints through `infer_model` and pydantic-ai warns that the existing `openai:` prefix will change meaning in v2 from Chat Completions to Responses. Choosing a replacement prefix is behavioral, not a mechanical deprecation cleanup.\n\n**A — Preserve Chat Completions (recommended):** change rebar-owned model construction to `openai-chat:`. This preserves today's wire protocol and broad custom-endpoint compatibility; held-out provider-parity tests must prove no outbound payload change.\n\n**B — Migrate to Responses:** use `openai-responses:` and intentionally adopt the newer API. This may change payloads, structured-output behavior, streaming, and endpoint compatibility; it requires explicit parity evidence and migration documentation.\n\n**C — Defer with a dependency bound:** retain `openai:` and pin pydantic-ai below v2 temporarily. This avoids an immediate behavior choice but carries upgrade debt and leaves the warning unresolved.\n\nRecommendation: approve A unless there is a product goal to adopt Responses now. No code, claim, or implementation work will begin until the user selects the intended behavior."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786914967354109001,"uuid":"7f5b9c76-08e7-4e57-be31-2eb4719f93e0"}